# Same molecule/basis as h2.inp, but with an extreme speed of light. Unlike
# water-c10000000.inp (STO-3G, a small/minimal basis), this combination
# hits a much more severe numerical breakdown at the same c: cc-pVTZ's
# larger, more flexible Small-component basis leaves S_small's inverse
# square root far worse conditioned, so by c=1e7 the Kramers-pair
# splitting check reaches ~140 hartree (not just small rounding noise) and
# the eigenvector-level Kramers check reaches ~1 (complete failure, not a
# tiny deviation). At this basis size, c=1e7 is simply too extreme to
# probe the nonrelativistic limit meaningfully; compare against a more
# moderate value (e.g. 1000), where both checks come out essentially
# perfect (~1e-6 and ~1e-16 respectively). This is a numerical-precision
# limitation of testing literal c -> infinity for a larger, more
# ill-conditioned basis, not a sign of a bug in the physics.
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
SPEED_OF_LIGHT = 10000000
NELEC 2
BASIS h2-cc-pvtz.gbs

GEOMETRY
H   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   0.741400
END
